WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.280
After first finding American fame on the goofy
'90s sitcom Two Guys, a Girl and a Pizza Place,

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.349
Ryan Reynolds moved on to play leading roles
in multiple romantic comedies as well as action

00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:14.059
flicks like Blade: Trinity, Green Lantern,
and—of course—Deadpool, the role he was

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:15.289
born to play.

00:00:15.289 --> 00:00:18.920
Reynolds always brings a playful edge and
sharp sense of humor to his roles, which can

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.110
lead to a lot of extra footage and hilarious
outtakes.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.029
Here are some of Ryan Reynolds' best bloopers.

00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:26.029
Deadpool

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:30.509
With Deadpool, Hollywood finally figured out
what to do with Ryan Reynolds.

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:34.380
The fictional character blended so seamlessly
with Reynolds' real-life sense of humor that

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.670
the movie relied heavily on Reynolds' improvisation.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:41.230
"It's very ice to see you.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.230
Schwarzenegger."

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.230
However, only one take of a scene can make
the final cut, meaning there's a lot of Deadpool

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.730
outtake footage.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.820
Before Wade Wilson becomes Deadpool, he submits
to some highly questionable medical experimentation.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.830
He keeps his spirits up by making fun of his
captors, which gives Reynolds a chance to

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.140
rattle off different insults.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.640
"You're gonna leave me all alone here with
Henry Winkler.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:03.310
You're gonna leave me alone with 'heyyyy you
guys!'

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.180
You're gonna leave me all alone here with
Chris Angel Mind Freak"

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.620
Then there's this scene, where Deadpool shows
up at the X-Men mansion and talks about the

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.030
joys of joining the team.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.330
"Yeah that's right I can't wait to join the
gang.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:18.760
I'll give Beast a nice little belly rub it's
gonna be great."

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.250
Blade: Trinity

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:25.640
What few comic moments there are in the dark
and violent conclusion to Wesley Snipes' vampire

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.970
hunter trilogy come courtesy of Ryan Reynolds,
even though Blade himself ignores most of

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:31.060
those jokes.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.060
In this blooper, director David S. Goyer let
Reynolds riff in character, describing his

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.990
character's musical tastes in the process.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:37.990
"Me?

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.130
I'm more of a Kenny G fan myself you know?

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.160
Early stuff though.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.760
before he sold out."

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.690
"Me, I'm more of a Clay Aiken fan.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.220
People say I look like him."

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:55.200
"Me, I'm more of a Don Johnson fan, most people
don't know that he recorded an album."

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.560
The Proposal

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.420
This 2009 rom-com starred three of Hollywood's
most well-liked actors: Sandra Bullock, Betty

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.020
White, and Ryan Reynolds.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.229
In one of the scenes, they all get together
for a group hug, which leads to one of the

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:07.890
best bloopers from the movie.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.469
"Still rolling!"

00:02:09.469 --> 00:02:13.040
"My nipple, she's got my nipple!"

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.980
Honestly, we can't tell if Reynolds is making
fun of Betty White's height, or if White actually

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.439
tried to take a bite out of him.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.439
Either way, at least they didn't start kissing.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.840
Nope, Reynolds saved all that loving for the
dog.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
The Hitman's Bodyguard

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.110
Regardless of your religion, nuns are generally
regarded as people you don't mess with.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.580
So of course, that's what Ryan Reynolds does.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.120
In one scene for The Hitman's Bodyguard, Reynolds
is in a bus with a bunch of clapping nuns.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:50.019
He waits for a quiet moment and launches a
clap attack on the one sitting right next

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:50.520
to him.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.230
The Change-Up

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.989
In this blooper from the body switch movie
The Change-Up, Reynolds reacts quickly when

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:06.659
he can't remember his lines.

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:10.451
He stays in character as long as he can before
admitting to costar Jason Bateman that he

00:03:10.451 --> 00:03:12.500
has no idea what he's supposed to be doing.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.340
"I don't feel particularly good about this."

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.840
"We're just doing a pickup?"

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.209
"No, I just had a complete brain malfunction."

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:19.739
"You want to reload?"

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.380
"Probably because I don't feel particularly
good about this."

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.700
Just Friends

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.459
Let's face it: Poop jokes can be pretty funny.

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:29.760
They're even funny on repeat—possibly even
funnier.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.510
Case in point: this blooper from the comedy
Just Friends.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.950
Each time Reynolds tries to say his ridiculous
line, he and costar Amy Smart just laugh harder

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.269
and harder.

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:41.269
"Leave?

00:03:41.269 --> 00:03:43.389
Why would Mr. Peepee pants want to leave?

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.389
Stick around.

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:46.939
I'm gonna s--- myself.

00:03:46.939 --> 00:03:47.939
Stick around.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.500
I'm gonna crap my pants.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.739
I'm gonna crap my pants!"

00:03:54.739 --> 00:03:57.249
R.I.P.D.

00:03:57.249 --> 00:04:00.790
It's nice to know that some actors never lose
their sense of fun while filming a movie.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.839
As this footage from the making of R.I.P.D.
shows, Reynolds always has a blast while making

00:04:04.839 --> 00:04:05.839
a film.

00:04:05.839 --> 00:04:09.370
Of course, it helps that he's got some fellow
goofballs like Jeff Bridges and Kevin Bacon

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.100
to play against—and a stunt car to mess
around in.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.220
"Everybody okay?"

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:20.460
Thanks for watching!

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.870
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.000
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

